From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:23:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mach: Run WPT on OpenHarmony devices with mach test-wpt
 --ohos

This replaces `./mach test-ohos-wpt`, which could only run a single test.

It refuses `--no-headless`, since the app on this stack can't run WPT yet,
and `./mach update-wpt` refuses logs of runs on OpenHarmony, whose results
would otherwise replace the Linux expectations.

Validation: the device runs of the previous patch went through `./mach test-wpt --ohos --release`, which picks the staged headless executable of the build type; with `--no-headless` it stops with an explanation, and `./mach update-wpt` with the log of such a run exits with an error without writing expectations. A QuickJS build (`./mach build --ohos --release --headless-binary --js-engine quickjs`) ran `/infrastructure/` and `/dom/nodes/` on the phone with `--js-engine quickjs`, which put `js_engine: quickjs` into the run info; its unexpected results equal SpiderMonkey's except that `allowed-to-play.html` hangs instead of crashing and one more test timed out under load. Desktop `./mach test-wpt --release` still runs the `servo` product with `js_engine: spidermonkey`. `./mach test-scripts` and `./mach test-tidy` pass.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also ran the checks above; the cherry-pick onto ohos-main kept both the new `--ohos` and the stack's `--js-engine` option of test-wpt; with fixes from an agent review)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
